the ordinary Metal preset leaves the narrow bias accumulation on one thread: true
at the lower mapping threshold the ordinary preset maps the bias channels: true
the untuned Metal plan splits the bias gradient into 32 blocks: true
the partials pass launches one thread per block and channel before the combine: true
the zero split threshold leaves the Metal bias reduction unsplit: true
disabling the split gives the ordinary bias gradient bitwise: true
the real untuned Metal compile ships the parallel partials pass and its combine: true
the ordinary bias gradient agrees with the f64 sum: true
the untuned bias gradient agrees with the f64 sum: true
